## Projector channels (`BirdEyeRouteProjector` + `BirdEyeRouteOverlay`)

Three independent overlay channels, projected each frame through the shared world-to-NDC pipeline:

| Channel | Public method | Rendered as |
|---|---|---|
| Primary NavMesh polyline | `on_route_computed(points_3d)` / `clear_route()` | Solid dashed line (RDP-simplified) |
| Auxiliary OSM polyline | `set_osm_segment(points_3d)` / `clear_osm_segment()` | Wider-gap dashed line, slightly paler ("this part will be auto-walked for you") |
| Solo pin marker | `set_pin_marker(world)` / `clear_pin_marker()` | Standalone flag bubble for the "pin sheet open, no route yet" state |

All three channels have independent lifetimes (the pin sheet may still be open after a navmesh route was cancelled; an OSM preview can live alongside a recalculating NavMesh leg). `clear_route()` does NOT wipe the pin marker or OSM segment — callers must clear each channel explicitly.

`_dispatch_if_empty()` emits one final empty payload when the last active channel clears so the client stops rendering the previous snapshot.

**Endpoint bubble logic (multi-segment):**
- Start bubble = first NavMesh point if any, else first OSM point.
- Destination bubble = last OSM point if any, else last NavMesh point.

