## Known limitations / future work

- **Magnet radius vs city clicks** — a large `MAX_MAGNET_SNAP_XZ_CM` keeps roof/centre picks on arena magnets; a click on nearby streets inside that radius still snaps to an arena waypoint. Tighten the constant or add a second rule (e.g. prim/bounds) if that becomes common.
- **Pause / resume positioning** — re-feeding the polyline from index 0 teleports the route cursor back to the start; the player walks back before resuming forward. Revisit with polyline trimming if it becomes annoying.
- **Arrival celebration for outside pins** — fires the generic POI celebration via `on_auto_move_complete`. A "you arrived at your pin" variant would be nicer.
- **Entrance spawn points** — Kit falls back to `PlayerSpawnPoint_Foyer` + teleport to the entrance when no specific start spawn is authored. If entrance-adjacent spawn points are added later, the panel could pass them as `startSpawnPoint` directly to skip the teleport.
- **Free-roam after OSM arrival** — players arrive at the pinned outside point off-mesh; no NavMesh there to walk on. Adding OSM-region NavMeshes for named sub-areas (and exposing them as additional composer islands) is the planned follow-up.
- **Island-aware entrance naming** — the composer reads the island from `nav_waypoint_entrance_<island>_<idx>` prim names. Entrance waypoints without an island prefix fall back to `DEFAULT_ISLAND = "scandinavium"` for backwards compatibility. New islands should adopt the prefixed convention from the start.

